---
const pillars = [
  {
    k: 'build',
    title: 'Real-time ML pipelines',
    body: 'End-to-end streaming systems, from acquisition through causal preprocessing to inference and a command to hardware, designed around latency budgets from day one.',
  },
  {
    k: 'measure',
    title: 'Benchmark before you believe',
    body: 'Every deep model is compared with classical baselines on accuracy, latency, stability and compute, so the model that ships is the one that earns its cost.',
  },
  {
    k: 'ship',
    title: 'AI-first engineering',
    body: 'I use agentic coding tools such as Claude Code across the stack, from pipelines and analysis to documentation, and review and test what they produce.',
  },
];
---

<section id="about" class="section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="container-x">
    <p class="eyebrow reveal">02 · How I build</p>
    <h2 id="about-title" class="h-section reveal">AI for messy, real-world <span class="text-gradient">sensor data.</span></h2>
    <p class="lede reveal">
      I'm a doctoral researcher at the University of Helsinki. My day job is turning noisy, high-dimensional
      signals into decisions a machine can act on in real time. Neuroscience taught me the hard data problems:
      drift, artefacts and tight latency. Now I build the AI systems that handle them, and I want to bring that
      to Earth observation and SAR.
    </p>

    <div class="pillars">
      {
        pillars.map((p) => (
          <article class="pillar glass reveal">
            <p class="mono k">{p.k}</p>
            <h3>{p.title}</h3>
            <p>{p.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <a class="next glass glass-hover reveal" href="#interests">
      <span class="next-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" /><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="10.5" ry="3.6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" transform="rotate(-20 12 12)" /></svg>
      </span>
      <span class="next-text">
        <span class="mono next-k">next orbit</span>
        <span class="next-t">Earth observation &amp; SAR</span>
        <span class="next-s">Foundational astrophysics and space coursework (ANU), plus a coherent-imaging background that maps onto radar.</span>
      </span>
      <span class="next-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

